READ-ONLY costing round. No package source touched, no version bump, no rc.

Four ops proposed, seven rejected, every number re-derived through the
prototypes and checked cell-by-cell against rc426's committed table:
40 comparisons, all EXACT.

THE CLASS ASSIGNMENT — verified, not adopted (the brief's ask):
* Class C on ORDER SURVIVES. The shipped `chiral_flip` IS the order-swap,
  bit-exact at word length 2 and 3 on all five carriers.
* Class K on INVERSION is REFUTED, twice. The shipped tree labels
  conjugation Class C four times (q8_conjugate, oct_conjugate,
  quaternion_conjugate, octonion_conjugate) and Class K twice
  (cd_conjugate and its private `_conj`) — and the two families each cite
  the other as "the discrete mirror" while carrying opposite labels. The
  executable test agrees: the shipped Class-K atoms reproduce inv(a) on
  1 element per carrier (the fixed point) and on TI24 cannot even be
  applied, because pin_slot_at_zero is a real-axis op and TI24's elements
  are pairs.
* "K THEN C" is EMPTY as a sequencing claim — invert-then-flip equals
  flip-then-invert on 100% of words on all five carriers, because the
  inversion is pointwise.
* The real reading is C-on-ORDER paired with the CARRIER'S OWN inverse
  class, which is C on Q8/O16 and I on the cyclic and T/I carriers.

WHY IT IS NOT A WRAPPER: `chiral_dual(pointwise_inverse, ·)` equals the
inversion with NO order reversal on 100% of words. Its two flips cancel
around any pointwise op, so the nearest shipped composition returns the
WRONG object by construction, not by omission.

THE SET INSTRUMENT: at O16 both readings score bare == chiral == 2752 on
sets differing by 1344 triples in EACH direction. The deliberately blind
count-only control blesses them as equal, and is wrong — which is the
control passing by failing.

THE RATE THAT IS THREE RATES: rc426 emits a record kind named
`bare_rate_is_commuting_probability`. On the four groups the identity is
real. At the loop they are THREE different rationals — bare 43/64,
Pr(G) 11/32, k/|G| 9/16 — and the committed record shows only two of
them, so the first link's failure is invisible. The two land on OPPOSITE
sides of 5/8. Corrected here rather than inherited.

GUSTAFSON: the bibliography entry and d(Q8) = 5/8 are VERIFIED-SELF from
a PDF fetched and extracted in session (arXiv:1001.4856, Hofmann-Russo,
Example 4.1 p.13 and reference [8] p.16 — whose page range carries a
typo, reported not corrected). The BOUND ITSELF is not stated there, the
1973 Monthly note is JSTOR-paywalled and therefore REJECTED as
attestation, and the only source that states it attaches a blog. Shipped
as DERIVED-AND-MEASURED: a four-step derivation with every step executed
on every carrier. It gets verdict FIELDS on op 4, not a constant-op.

